# Connection Pool Learning Notes

## Self-Assessment Questions & Answers

### Q1: Why use channel instead of slice for pool?
Channels provide built-in synchronization and natural blocking.

```go
// Slice (BAD): needs mutex, manual blocking
mu.Lock()
conn := slice[0]
slice = slice[1:]
mu.Unlock()

// Channel (GOOD): no mutex, blocks automatically
conn := <-p.conns  // Blocks if empty!
```

---

### Q2: How do you detect a dead connection?
Call `IsValid()` before returning connection from Acquire:
```go
conn := <-p.conns
if !conn.IsValid() {
    conn.Close()       // Destroy dead connection
    <-p.semaphore      // Release semaphore slot
    return p.Acquire() // Retry
}
return conn
```

---

### Q3: What happens if Release is called twice?

**Problem:** Same connection ends up in pool twice!
```go
Release(conn)  // 1st: conn added to pool
Release(conn)  // 2nd: SAME conn added again!
               // Now 2 Acquire() get same conn!
```

**Solution:** Track released state:
```go
type PooledConn struct {
    Conn
    released bool
}

func Release(conn *PooledConn) {
    if conn.released {
        return  // Ignore duplicate
    }
    conn.released = true
    // ...
}
```

---

### Q4: Why semaphore in addition to conns channel?

```
conns channel:     Stores IDLE connections
semaphore channel: Tracks TOTAL connections (created - destroyed)
```

```
Scenario: maxSize = 3

After 3 Acquires:
  conns:     [] (empty)
  semaphore: [x, x, x] (full - at max)

After 1 Release:
  conns:     [conn1] (1 idle)
  semaphore: [x, x, x] (still full)

After destroy:
  semaphore: [x, x] (slot freed - can create new)
```

---

## Key Patterns Learned

### 1. Channel as Connection Store
```go
type Pool struct {
    conns chan Conn  // Buffered channel holds idle connections
}

conn := <-pool.conns  // Acquire (blocks if empty)
pool.conns <- conn    // Release
```

### 2. Semaphore for Max Connections
```go
semaphore := make(chan struct{}, maxSize)

// Create: acquire slot
semaphore <- struct{}{}
conn := factory()

// Destroy: release slot
<-semaphore
```

### 3. Context-Based Timeout
```go
select {
case conn := <-p.conns:
    return conn
case <-ctx.Done():
    return nil, ErrTimeout
}
```

